# YUI Project Changelog

All notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.

The format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.1.0/),
and this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).

## [Unreleased]

### Added

- Local models (Ollama and other OpenAI-compatible servers): Thinking can be turned off for much
  faster replies, and Temperature and Repetition Penalty can be set (Cardinal System).
- Action Mode: desktop actions as tags (default, best for local models) or as the server's tool
  calling (Tools, for large models; OpenAI-compatible servers for now). A server that rejects tools
  falls back to tags by itself.
- Authority Level (was Small Model Mode): Limited, for small local models, keeps Yui to company only (no actions) with a short reminder in every message.
- The System Console log can show every request to the AI (without the access key) and its raw reply.
- Message windows show a little Markdown: bold, inline code, bullets, headings and code blocks.
- MHCP Profile (Cardinal System, Personality): keep your own personalities (Save As…, Rename…,
  Delete) and switch between them and the built-in MHCP001. An edited personality becomes the
  profile "Custom".
- More System Call spells: Enhance Armament (Yui glows), Release Recollection (a burst that shakes
  her), Transfer Durability (she reports the computer's loads).
- Login Greeting: good morning on the first morning of a day, and long time no see after three days
  or more away.
- Recollection Log (Yui's Heart, Local Memory): search it as you type, and export it as a text file.
- Navigation Reports also warn about a nearly full system drive (System Console: Storage Capacity)
  and a lost network (Network Link), and tell you when it is back.
- Boss Raid: focus time with Yui (25 minutes by default, then a 5-minute rest). Start it from her
  menu or ask her; meanwhile the crystal turns violet and she does not speak up by herself.
- Col Ledger (System Console, Monitor): this month's tokens as the servers report them, with an
  optional Monthly Budget (Advanced) that Yui warns about once a month.
- Mental Record (Yui's Heart): once a day Yui asks how you feel and records it; the last 30 days
  as a chart. After a few low days she cares more (Daily Mood Check in Mental Health Counseling).
**Link Start**: when the widget starts, Yui's Heart glows, bursts into motes of light and Yui grows out of the flash (as the crystal form, the motes gather into it instead); no sound of its own, SAO Utils plays its "Link Start!". Always on (Test Link Start in System Console replays it). Switching between the crystal and the character in Equipment plays a transition of its own and keeps her size.
**Bond** (Yui's Heart): Player Birthday and Meeting Day (the first day by default); Yui celebrates the birthday and each anniversary once that day.
**Mental Health Counseling** window (Yui's task as MHCP-001), from her menu: Counseling (Login Greeting, Rest Reminders — formerly Mental Health Counseling —, Daily Mood Check, Spontaneous Talk, moved from Cardinal System's Pixie Functions), Mental Record and Bond (moved from Yui's Heart). Boss Raid stays in Pixie Functions for now.
**Navigation Reports** moved to System Console's Monitor, next to the thresholds and Report Interval; **Close Programs** (Authority) is off by default.
**Core Tuning**: Top P, Top K, Frequency Penalty and Seed, each sent only where the server takes it; **Thinking Depth** (Off / Default / Low / Medium / High) replaces the Thinking switch and now reaches Claude and Gemini too (thinking budget).
Tags without a value (<<happy>>) are no longer shown; an expression name counts as the expression.
**SAO Utils action and data**: MHCP-YUI can be bound in the launcher, menus, other widgets' buttons and shortcuts (Open Chat with an optional message, Spontaneous Talk, Start / End Boss Raid, open each window), and her values (Companion Days, Today's Mood, Col Ledger, Boss Raid minutes left, Heart Core) can be shown by HP bars and HUD widgets.
**Skill Slots** window: Boss Raid (moved from Pixie Functions, with its status and a start / end button), **Alarm** (reminders by <<remind:time|text>> or by hand, once or daily, kept across restarts, missed ones told at start) and **Quest Log** (notes and to-dos by <<note:>> / <<done:>> or by hand, sent to Yui only when asked about, exportable); in the action (Skill Slots) and the data (Next Alarm).
**Weekly Report** (Mental Health Counseling): Yui looks back on the last seven days (chats, moods, Boss Raids, finished to-dos) and writes a few words about the week, on request or by herself on Sunday evenings (Sunday Report); reports are kept.
**Ollama (local)** server preset: the local address filled in, no access key needed, Scan Cores lists the installed models.
**Sword Skills** (Skill Slots): five slots, each a name and any SAO Utils action (a Script Action chains several steps); Yui runs one when you ask for it by name (<<skill:>>), after you confirm. **Weather Report** (Mental Health Counseling): weather and temperature from a SAO Utils data source (e.g. Weather Data), mentioned in the morning greeting (umbrella when it rains) and used for weather questions.
Settings grouped by what they do: Mental Health Counseling in Companion (Login Greeting, Spontaneous Talk, Weather Report), Care (Rest Reminders, Daily Mood Check, Sunday Report), Bond and Records (moods and weekly reports, no settings); Skill Slots tabs show their settings first, then the status or lists under a heading.
Entry points: the right-click menu holds the settings windows only; the MHCP-YUI action gains Start / End Boss Raid, Add Reminder, Remove Next Reminder, Add Note, Finish First Note, Record Mood, Write Weekly Report and Run Sword Skill; the data gains text values (Quest Log, Next Alarm, Boss Raid Timer, Today's Mood, Latest Weekly Report) for HUD text; **Yui · Menu** Quick Menu preset (crystal icon, SAO style).
The MHCP-YUI action is split into categories like other extensions' actions: Chat, Boss Raid, Alarm, Quest Log, Mental Record, Sword Skills and Windows (nvg://yui.widget.amarsimos.com/action#chat…); each shows only its own settings.
**Quick input** at the cursor for actions that need something each time: Add Reminder... (text, +10 / +30 / +60 or a time such as 明天 8:00, 周五 15:00), Add Note..., Record Mood... (stars and a note), Start Boss Raid with 0 minutes (15 / 25 / 45 / 60); Ask Yui hands it to the chat. The actions no longer have text settings. Reminder times also take 明天 / 后天 / 周X.
Fewer action categories: Yui (Open Chat, Spontaneous Talk, Record Mood..., Write Weekly Report), Skill Slots (Boss Raid, reminders, notes, sword skills) and Windows.
**Raid Banner** (Skill Slots, Boss Raid): the time left in big white SAO letters over a notched white bar, on top of the screen and dragged anywhere; when the raid is won, "Congratulations!!" across the screen as when a floor boss falls, then the rest the same way; Show Raid Banner in the Skill Slots action.
**Raid Banner** effects: a white flash, "Congratulations!!" lighting letter by letter, light motes drifting up and a sound (the HUD preset is gone again; the Raid Cleared data stays).
The small tools (Skill Slots: Boss Raid, Alarm, Quest Log, Sword Skills, with their actions, data, tags and the Raid Banner) are set aside until they become extensions of their own; their data is kept.
Every button of the settings windows is centered (Reset This Tab too); rows of buttons wrap within the page when narrow (CenteredFlow).
**Character Traits** (Cardinal System, Personality): Warmth, Energy, Kaomoji, Reply Length (less / default / more) and Format (chat / lists), added to the personality; **Quick Replies**: two or three short replies under Yui's latest message, sent with a click (<<suggest:>>); **Log Recall** (Yui's Heart, Recall): related older chat messages from the recollection log read with each request (found locally); **Through Yui's Eyes** (Yui's Heart, Memories): Yui sums up what her memories say of you.
Yui's Heart, Memories reworked: Through Yui's Eyes as a card folded to three lines, Heart Core / Fragments tabs with counts and the search, each memory a card (orange stripe for the core, grey for fragments, when noted and how often recalled) whose edit / pin / move / delete buttons appear on hover, multi-line editing, and adding at the bottom.
Settings windows under headings: Cardinal System keeps the AI itself in Link (Server, Core, Connection Test; Reset This Tab keeps the access key), Core Tuning (Reply, Sampling, Behavior; the sampling values in a Sampling Parameters dialog) and Personality (Identity, MHCP Profile, Character Traits; the traits in a Fine-Tuning dialog). Pixie Functions is gone: Standby Mode is in Mental Health Counseling (Companion: Greeting, Presence, Weather), External Browser and the search engine in System Console (Authority: Actions, Browsing, File Search, Delete Authority, Immortal Objects). System Console's Monitor has Load (thresholds in a Crystal Thresholds dialog), Navigation Reports and Col Ledger, its Log the tests in a Run a Test dialog; Yui's Heart has Memory, Context and Chat History (Recall), Transfer and Backup (Local Memory). **Thinking Depth** moved to Core Tuning and is Off by default. Settings pages scroll to their end at any window height.
Memories keep their dates: relative days written by Yui ("明天考试") are turned into dates when saved, a bare date or time is not kept, and every memory reaches the AI with the day it was noted ([10-12] ...).
Replies of small local models cleaned up: thinking written into the reply (before </think>) and repeated paragraphs are left out, tags closed by a single ">" are understood, and quick replies split by "/" or "、" too.
**Now Playing** (Mental Health Counseling, Companion, Music; needs the Media Player package): Yui knows the song in the player and can talk about it; **Control Media** (System Console, off by default) lets her play, pause, skip and change the volume through Media Player's own action.
**Care Scheduler**: everything Yui says by herself (late-night care, rest reminders, the Sunday Report, Spontaneous Talk) goes through one scheduler that says at most one thing at a time, within a daily number and a gap set by **Care Level** (Mental Health Counseling, Care: Auto learns from your responses, 20 a day and once every half hour to start; or Quiet, Normal, Chatty) and outside **Quiet Hours** (no small talk, 00:00–08:00 by default, SAO Utils' time pickers). Telling her to be quiet stops her for the day; asking her to talk more makes her talk more.
Honest actions: a reply that says Yui did something on the computer when nothing was carried out, or promises a reminder she cannot give, gets a note under it; she is told what she can and cannot do.
**Follow-ups** (Mental Health Counseling, Care, on by default): when Yui remembers something with a date to come (an exam, an interview), she cheers you on that day and asks how it went in the week after (08:00–22:00), by herself or beside your own message; Yui's Heart lists them on its new Follow-ups page, where Remove stops one and keeps the memory. System Console's Follow-up: Today / After try it at once.
**Now**: every request ends with one line of what is true right now (time and part of the day, how long Yui has been awake with you, how long since you last talked, the weather, the song, a high load, today's mood, a birthday or anniversary), so Yui knows them all the time; the prompt is shorter than the separate paragraphs it replaces.
**Mood Care** and **Weather Changes** (Mental Health Counseling, Care): after three low moods Yui gently asks if you want to talk; when it starts to rain or snow, or gets 5° colder, she tells you. Spontaneous Talk often starts from something of right now (a holiday, a year ago today, a day soon, the song, a busy computer, meals, weekends, the cold...). Woken up after a while, she greets you as at start-up; long time no see after two days.
**Unread**: when Yui says something while the chat is closed and you miss it, her collapsed form keeps a mark (the crystal's heart blinks slowly and a blue dot breathes; a dot beside the pixie or the character) until you open the chat or click the bubble; the chat then opens at a "New messages" line, her unread messages lined in SAO orange.

### Changed

- While the chat is closed, everything Yui says (replies, care reminders, load and battery warnings)
  appears in the speech bubble next to her collapsed form, pixie and avatar too, instead of SAO Utils
  notifications. While the chat is open it is only in the chat. The crystal's load tooltip is gone.
- The chat, the speech bubble and Seedling widgets follow the widget's display settings: shown in the
  launcher or on the desktop as the widget is (also when the launcher opens and closes), and on top
  or not as the widget is. The chat remembers where it is relative to Yui, the same in both.
- The speech bubble keeps clear of the widget's drag bar.
- The settings windows are in tabs, with only the basic settings shown: Advanced in the title bar
  shows the rest, Help the explanations, Reset restores the window and Reset This Tab one tab (the
  ↺ beside each setting is gone). System Console has Monitor, Authority and Log tabs, the log filling
  the window. All settings use SAO Utils' own controls: sliders show their value while dragged,
  number boxes take typed values (Reply Length Limit, Standby Mode, Spontaneous Talk), and Message
  Font is SAO Utils' font picker (family, size and style).
- Chat panel and bubble opacity go down to 0 (only their background; the text stays).
- Spontaneous Talk and the test bubble work in every collapsed form, not only the crystal.
- New default personality: shorter, with the most important rules first and without example lines
  that small models used to copy. **If you changed nothing in the personality, choose MHCP001 in
  Cardinal System's MHCP Profile to switch to the new one** (a saved personality is kept as it is).
- Yui no longer makes up real-time information such as the weather; she searches instead.
- Regenerating a reply asks for a different answer.
- No reply limit by default (OpenAI gets max_completion_tokens when one is set).
- Authority Level is Limited by default: with small models Yui keeps you company and does nothing
  on the computer; choose Full for large models. Search Files is off by default.
- Standby: Yui falls asleep when two things she says by herself go unanswered (you seem away), not
  after minutes without touching her; the Standby Mode setting is gone.
- Spontaneous Talk is a switch; how often she talks is Care Level's.
- Regenerate is called Say Again and keeps the facts (song, time, memories) while wording it anew.
- Quick Replies are only talk, never asking Yui to do something on the computer.
- Clear Log (Yui's Heart) clears the chat window too.
- **Yui's Heart** is a briolette like the pendant in the anime: a sky-blue teardrop covered in diamond
  facets, lit as a real solid and turning slowly. The status color is in the glow and the heart inside,
  which beats faster while she is busy.
- The speech bubble pops up with the message sound; its strip breathes and is sky blue, yellow or red
  only when the crystal warns.
- Mental Health Counseling: Perception (what Yui knows: the weather, the song) and Care (when she speaks
  up: Frequency, Greeting, Small Talk, Well-being, Your Days, Reports). System Console's tests are in
  three groups: Actions, Care, Display.
- Yui always starts collapsed, even if the chat was open when SAO Utils closed.
- Care Tick (System Console) always makes her say something, Quiet Hours and today's number aside.

### Fixed

- The speech bubble's text uses the Message Font: on a Japanese system it mixed glyphs of different
  fonts and weights.
- Misspelled or full-width tags (for example <<emphy:happy>>) are no longer shown in the chat.
- The System Console log's scroll bar is at the right, as tall as the log, and can be dragged.
- When the reply names no expression, Yui guesses one from it.

## [1.1.0] - 2026-10-20

### Added

- Chat in its own window, styled as an SAO message panel: opens and closes with SAO animations,
  can be resized and moved by dragging its title or Yui herself, and is closed by clicking its
  title, Yui's image or with Esc.
- Messages as SAO instant message windows; while Yui thinks, "YUI正在思考" with hints.
- ↑ / ↓ in the input box bring back the messages you sent before, also after a restart.
- Widget presets: "Yui · Navigation Pixie" and "Yui · Heart Crystal".
- Yui's Heart Crystal: a collapsed form colored by CPU, GPU and memory load, with a speech bubble.
- Desktop actions: Yui can start programs, find files (Everything) and close programs, always
  after your confirmation. Protected system processes are never closed.
- Yui's Heart window with three pages: Memories (add and edit), Recall (Auto Memory, heart core
  size, how much is sent) and Local Memory (export, import, daily backups, chat log, forget all).
- System Console (formerly Option): load monitor, desktop action permissions, test buttons and log.
- New settings: reply length limit, search engine, bubble time and opacity, chat panel opacity,
  sounds, load report interval and Spontaneous Talk.
- ↺ next to each setting restores its default; Reset restores a whole window after confirming.

### Changed

- Settings take effect immediately (no Save button).
- New defaults: transparent Field, Yui01 as the pixie, Source Han Sans for messages.
- Setting names are in English in every language; descriptions are translated.
- Confirmations that delete something use the system alert sound.
- Your messages are titled Papa or Mama.
- Seedling (the widget lab) is hidden for now.

### Fixed

- A frame of the old chat flashed when reopening it quickly.
- Console windows appeared when a widget was added.
- Values at the right edge of settings were cut off; settings no longer scroll sideways.

## [1.0.0] - 2026-10-15

### Added

- AI providers: OpenAI, Google Gemini, DeepSeek, Kimi (Moonshot), Anthropic Claude and a
  custom OpenAI-compatible server, picked as Seed Server + Core Program. Each server keeps its
  own model, address and access key.
- Scan Cores: fetch the current model list from the server; Manual Core ID for any model id.
- Streaming replies (text appears as it is generated), with Cancel to stop a reply and a
  regenerate button on Yui's last reply.
- Conversation memory: recent messages are sent as context, and the last 50 messages are kept
  across restarts.
- Yui knows the current date and time.
- Multi-line input: Enter sends, Shift+Enter starts a new line.
- Registered Parent: Yui calls you Papa or Mama.
- Yui's Heart: long-term memories Yui saves herself, viewable and editable in the Cardinal
  System dialog.
- Emotion Display: Yui changes her expression with the mood of each reply (optional images).
- Navigation Pixie Form: with a pixie image set, Yui turns into a small hovering pixie while the
  message window is hidden.
- Standby Mode: Yui falls asleep when two things she says by herself go unanswered (you seem away); click her or write to her to wake her up.
- Login Greeting: Yui welcomes you back after you have been away.
- Mental Health Counseling: reminders to sleep late at night and to rest after long sessions.
- Navigation Reports: warnings about low battery and high CPU or memory usage.
- Navigation: Yui can offer to open a page or a search; it is confirmed in SAO Utils' system
  message box and opened by SAO Utils (or the system browser with External Browser on).
- "System Call" easter egg: Sacred Arts element commands from Alicization.
- SAO-style scroll bars and a comic-style tail on Yui's message bubbles.
- Message font size setting.
- Translations: all interface text can be localized (`i18n/`, `Locales/`); Chinese descriptions
  are included.

### Changed

- Settings renamed after SAO: "Cardinal System" (formerly Core Settings) and "Equipment"
  (formerly Style Settings), with a description under each setting.
- The character image keeps its aspect ratio and is centered; the message window fills the
  remaining width. Minimum size: 300 x 400 for the character, room for the input row beside it.
- Hiding the message window shrinks the widget to the character and showing it restores the
  previous size; the widget can still be resized either way.
- Error messages are written in Yui's voice.
- Fonts are saved by name instead of list position.
- Settings from 0.0.2 (API key, endpoint and model) are migrated automatically.

### Fixed

- The selected model did not match the model actually sent to the API.
- A custom API endpoint was overwritten when switching models.
- The settings dialogs could only be opened once.
- The background image setting had no effect, and a chosen Field background reset to the
  default after a restart (set it again once after updating).
- Long text without spaces overflowed the message bubbles; replies could be shown as rich text.
- The chat did not always scroll to the newest message.
- Requests that never answered left the chat stuck; they now time out.

## [0.0.2] - 2025-12-24

### Changed

- Updated README.md
- Optimized Settings UI
- Optimized code logic

## [0.0.1] - 2025-12-22

### Added

- Initial release of YUI Project
